[TITLE]
Disconnected island -> Error 110 (all-default hydraulic options)
Island = J3,J4 (ZERO demand), joined by 12 parallel OPEN pipes, cut off from
the reservoir by CLOSED pipes PC1,PC2. At trial 2 the island pipes carry
near-zero flow so each gets conductance capped at Hexp/RQtol ~ 1.852e7;
12 in parallel ~ 2.22e8, while the closed pipes couple the island to the
rest at only 1/CBIG = 1e-8. The exact Schur-complement pivot for the second
island node is ~2e-8, below one ulp of 2.22e8 (~3e-8), so floating-point
cancellation in sparse Cholesky drives it non-positive -> linsolve reports
ill-conditioning -> Error 110. (A single internal open pipe does NOT fail:
its pivot residual 2e-8 exceeds the ~2e-9 rounding at the 1.852e7 scale.)

